WEBVTT

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:10.900
Yugi Muto assembled the Millennium Puzzle and became the guardian of the Shadow Games.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:17.260
Pegasus has a Millennium Item of his own - the Millennium Eye.

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:21.800
Yugi accepts Pegasus's challenge and goes to Duelist Kingdom.

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:28.010
Pegasus stole his grandfather Sugoroku's soul, and Yugi intends to rescue him.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:33.850
He battles alongside his trusted friends and with his other self.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:44.300
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:51.210
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:57.960
Game cartridges are stacked in the corner of the room

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:04.660
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:09.760
You're on the other side of the table

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:13.130
I'm talking to you, but...

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:20.060
You don't change your facial expression at all

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:26.310
Even though I'm this close to you

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:33.580
These feelings don't reach you, don't reach you

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:40.320
What is truly precious?

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:54.400
The three gods of thunder, water and wind!

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:58.730
Combine your powers and resurrect with a roar!

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:00.030
What's that?

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:06.840
Come out, Gate Guardian!

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:12.080
Since you combined, we'll fight back with teamwork!  Here we go!

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:13.110
Bring it on!

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:19.120
The Fiend Dragon
B. Skull Dragon

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:25.660
There's nowhere to run!  What should I do, Yugi?

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:28.370
Lightning Shot!

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:34.270
It'll be destroyed!

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:41.100
Good.  Flame Swordsman is destroyed.

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:42.650
Are you sure?

00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:43.510
What?

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:47.930
The trap card Mirror Force.

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:50.520
It protects Flame Swordsman.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:51.520
Yugi!

00:02:55.750 --> 00:03:01.030
Gate Guardian, reflect it!  Storm Barricade!

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:04.020
Gate Guardian is...

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:05.570
...invincible.

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:11.000
But your other monster can't escape the attack.

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:17.740
Monster Tamer is destroyed.

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:19.900
How dare you!

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:25.520
Keep it up, you two!

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:28.340
Yeah!  Don't let your guard down, Jonouchi!

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:29.820
Got it!

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:35.240
Find him?

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:38.830
No, he's not over here.

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:41.830
He's still hiding in the basement somewhere.

00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:45.040
We'll guard Mokuba's cell.

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:47.440
You keep searching for Kaiba.

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:48.240
Understood.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:00.160
Okay, it's my turn.

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:02.920
Jonouchi, look at that monster's body.

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:06.120
Thunder, wind and water.

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:08.690
Each section can launch an attack.

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:12.320
If we destroy each section one at a time, we can defeat it!

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:15.130
You're right.

00:04:15.130 --> 00:04:16.620
It's my turn!

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:21.000
Flame Swordsman, use Salamandra's fire to attack Kazejin!

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:27.400
Go!

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:30.320
What?

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:38.060
You fool.  Don't underestimate our combined monster.

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:39.460
My turn!

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:42.020
Counterattack Flame Swordsman!

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:43.430
Tidal Wave!

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:49.030
This is bad.

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:54.370
Magical Hats protects Dark Magician from attacks.

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:56.430
But that's not the case for Flame Swordsman.

00:04:56.430 --> 00:05:00.160
Since it's a Water attack, it loses 300 attack points.

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:05.960
Flame Swordsman is destroyed.

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:06.650
Damn!

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:12.520
We were about to escape the Laybrinth!

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:14.800
Actually, this turn didn't go to waste.

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:18.500
It's my turn.  I set one card.

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:22.970
I summon Summoned Skull and follow the path that Flame Swordsman laid out.

00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:31.460
But its attack...

00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:35.130
...won't make it through the Labyrinth to reach Gate Guardian.

00:05:35.130 --> 00:05:35.850
Never.

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:38.100
Are you sure?

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:42.830
I told you that there's a path in the Labyrinth.

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:45.060
Look!

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:50.830
The Labyrinth is flooded.  Therefore...

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:54.730
Go!  Magic Lightning!

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:01.110
You did it!

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:03.420
You're wasting your time.

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:06.660
You can't get through Gate Guardian's defenses.

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:10.800
Winds will blow away the water!  Reflection!

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:14.640
What's wrong?

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:19.900
Too bad, but you recently attacked my Dark Magician hiding inside Magical Hats.

00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:23.060
So a trap card activated.

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:24.260
What?

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:29.130
I placed Spellbinding Circle on Dark Magician.

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:31.240
A trap card?

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:36.810
Spellbinding Circle stops the attack and lowers its attack points by 700.

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:45.560
The water section is destroyed!

00:06:45.560 --> 00:06:46.860
Serves you right!

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:50.000
The Thunder Attribute worked to our advantage!

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:52.000
Hooray!

00:06:57.290 --> 00:07:01.030
We'll knock each section down one at a time!

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:04.200
My turn.  I play Remove Trap.

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:06.630
This removes Spellbinding Circle.

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:10.930
Gate Guardian is back in control!

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:12.500
It's your turn.

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:14.310
My turn.

00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:20.320
Jonouchi, now's the time to play our trump card.

00:07:21.850 --> 00:07:23.820
I play this card!

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:26.730
Red-Eyes B. Dragon!

00:07:36.460 --> 00:07:42.860
I use the spell card Polymerization to fuse it with Summoned Skull.

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:46.400
That's...

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:49.700
The fiend dragon...

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:51.930
B. Skull Dragon!

00:07:56.560 --> 00:07:59.120
This is our team's strongest monster!

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:03.000
What will you do, Labyrinth Brothers?

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:10.800
Why are you both laughing?

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:14.830
You fools.  There's nothing you can do with that monster.

00:08:14.830 --> 00:08:16.130
Exactly.

00:08:16.130 --> 00:08:21.810
B. Skull Dragon can fly, but it can't fly through a Labyrinth.

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:24.500
Oh no!  It can't fly here!

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:26.260
That's right.

00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:30.400
You can only travel by foot inside a Labyrinth Field.

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:34.360
Yugi, I played it without thinking.

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:35.620
What should we do?

00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:37.830
Don't worry.  I have a plan.

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:40.460
I knew I could count on you.

00:08:40.730 --> 00:08:42.970
I end my turn.

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:05.830
It's my turn.

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:10.660
I drew a scary card.

00:09:12.060 --> 00:09:14.070
The spell card Riryoku!

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:16.120
Riryoku?

00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:18.240
You know that card?

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:22.130
It's a legendary super rare card.

00:09:22.760 --> 00:09:24.060
That's right.

00:09:24.060 --> 00:09:31.860
This card takes half your life points and adds it to my monsters' attack points.

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:34.530
What?  Half our life points?

00:09:34.530 --> 00:09:35.320
This is bad!

00:09:35.320 --> 00:09:36.600
And...

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:39.960
...Gate Guardian gains attack points!

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:45.160
Oh no.

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:46.700
This is bad.

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:51.460
Since I used Riryoku, I'm not allowed to attack this turn.

00:09:51.460 --> 00:09:59.220
But by combining Sanga and Kazejin's attack strength next turn, its destructive power will be devastating.

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:03.220
No matter what you try, you're finished next turn.

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:07.290
Jonouchi, I told you that I have a plan.

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:08.590
It's my turn.

00:10:11.530 --> 00:10:16.830
I'll make sure Dark Magician escapes this Labyrinth during this turn.

00:10:18.830 --> 00:10:21.800
Dark Magician, move six spaces forward.

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:25.330
You fool.

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:31.700
Even if you escape the Labyrinth, Gate Guardian's attack awaits you.

00:10:33.210 --> 00:10:40.820
Listen.  No matter what danger await us, we keep moving forward if we have a chance to win!

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:44.400
It has exited the Labyrinth.

00:10:45.820 --> 00:10:48.690
Then I play this card.

00:10:48.860 --> 00:10:50.360
Monster Reborn.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:55.550
No matter what monster you resurrect, it's pointless.

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:57.500
It's my turn.

00:10:57.500 --> 00:11:01.420
Gate Guardian attacks Dark Magician!

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:03.220
Combine your attacks!

00:11:03.220 --> 00:11:05.400
Magic Wind Shockwave!

00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:14.420
If I destroy Dark Magician, Yugi will have 0 life points.

00:11:14.420 --> 00:11:16.460
We win.

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:18.540
Your attack won't work.

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:20.900
Suijin, Reflection!

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:24.100
What?

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:30.340
The wall of water negates Magic Wind Shockwave.

00:11:33.030 --> 00:11:36.930
You used Monster Reborn to resurrect Suijin.

00:11:36.930 --> 00:11:39.230
And added it to your team.

00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:45.330
Awesome, Yugi!  I didn't think of that!

00:11:46.400 --> 00:11:48.260
They managed to survive.

00:11:48.260 --> 00:11:49.230
But...

00:11:50.130 --> 00:11:52.860
They survived this turn, but...

00:11:53.090 --> 00:11:58.170
Now our attacks won't hit them.

00:11:58.170 --> 00:12:01.030
It's your turn, Jonouchi.

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:02.060
Yeah.

00:12:02.060 --> 00:12:05.870
I know there has to be a way that we can win.

00:12:06.430 --> 00:12:10.960
They will definitely attack Suijin next turn.

00:12:10.960 --> 00:12:14.880
Then we won't be able to block their attacks anymore.

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:18.900
It all comes down to which card Jonouchi draws.

00:12:22.430 --> 00:12:24.940
Copycat?

00:12:24.940 --> 00:12:28.130
It copies my opponent's card?

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:34.960
I thought of a good idea!

00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:40.600
I change this card to Riryoku!

00:12:43.710 --> 00:12:49.960
I take half your life points and transform them into attack points!

00:12:50.220 --> 00:12:52.580
For B. Skull Dragon!

00:12:55.480 --> 00:12:56.760
Jonouchi!

00:12:57.520 --> 00:12:59.830
You fool.  How many times do I have to tell you?

00:12:59.830 --> 00:13:03.530
B. Skull Dragon cannot get through the Laybrinth.

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:05.260
It's my turn.

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:09.760
Kazejin attacks Suijin!

00:13:11.070 --> 00:13:13.330
Suijin, Reflection!

00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:20.930
I knew you would do that.

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:23.850
Take this!  Lightning Shot!

00:13:30.500 --> 00:13:31.630
Why did that happen?

00:13:31.630 --> 00:13:35.630
Suijin can only use Reflection once per turn.

00:13:39.860 --> 00:13:44.560
Yugi, you can no longer stop our attacks.

00:13:44.560 --> 00:13:47.010
We will win next turn.

00:13:48.200 --> 00:13:54.010
You still haven't realized why I had Dark Magician exit the Labyrinth?

00:13:54.230 --> 00:13:55.800
What?

00:13:55.800 --> 00:13:58.520
The spell card Monster Replace.

00:13:58.520 --> 00:14:05.890
It switches my monsters' positions, putting the one with the most attack points in front.

00:14:05.890 --> 00:14:07.420
It can't be...

00:14:07.420 --> 00:14:14.400
If their monster exits the Labyrinth, it can switch places with another monster.

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:15.830
Here we go!

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:35.520
Without Suijin, your Gate Guardian isn't strong enough to stop our powered-up B. Skull Dragon.

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:36.960
Meteor Flare!

00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:50.560
How's that!

00:14:50.560 --> 00:14:52.000
We win.

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:53.100
Woohoo!

00:14:53.100 --> 00:14:54.400
They did it!

00:14:54.400 --> 00:14:55.530
That means...

00:14:55.530 --> 00:14:56.930
Yugi and Jonouchi...

00:14:56.930 --> 00:14:59.500
Each have ten Star Chips!

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:00.660
All right!

00:15:00.660 --> 00:15:02.820
We can enter the castle!

00:15:04.160 --> 00:15:05.600
The game...

00:15:05.600 --> 00:15:07.230
...isn't over.

00:15:07.230 --> 00:15:08.560
What?

00:15:16.200 --> 00:15:17.300
What's wrong?

00:15:29.630 --> 00:15:32.510
Big brother, it's you!

00:15:32.510 --> 00:15:34.710
Mokuba, are you okay?

00:15:34.710 --> 00:15:40.040
Big brother!  I knew you'd come!

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:41.330
I knew it!

00:15:43.360 --> 00:15:45.640
Let's stay together forever.

00:15:45.640 --> 00:15:48.130
Yeah.  I promise.

00:15:49.100 --> 00:15:50.330
Mokuba.

00:15:51.430 --> 00:15:54.930
Big brother, I didn't give the key to anyone.

00:15:56.660 --> 00:15:57.840
Mokuba!

00:15:57.840 --> 00:16:00.760
I protected Kaiba Corporation.

00:16:00.760 --> 00:16:02.910
Just wait.  I'll get you out immediately.

00:16:07.580 --> 00:16:12.960
Bravo.  What a touching reunion.

00:16:13.270 --> 00:16:14.650
Pegasus.

00:16:14.650 --> 00:16:19.160
If you called in advance, I would have come to meet you.

00:16:20.360 --> 00:16:23.660
I didn't want to bother you.

00:16:24.260 --> 00:16:26.930
How modest of you.

00:16:26.930 --> 00:16:28.860
What do you mean?

00:16:29.260 --> 00:16:32.170
We'll give you all the Star Chips you want.

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:34.600
But did you forget?

00:16:34.600 --> 00:16:39.600
You haven't truly won until you make it out of this labyrinth.

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:40.960
I haven't forgotten.

00:16:40.960 --> 00:16:44.930
Tell us which door is the real exit.

00:16:44.930 --> 00:16:47.230
Go ahead and choose.

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:51.200
One door is the correct exit.

00:16:52.630 --> 00:16:57.600
This isn't fair!  Since you lost, tell us which one is the correct door!

00:16:57.600 --> 00:17:00.060
Which door will you pick?

00:17:00.060 --> 00:17:02.430
I knew this would happen.

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:05.100
Jonouchi, which is the correct door?

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:06.700
You expect me to know?

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:07.830
Nah.

00:17:09.030 --> 00:17:10.730
Yugi, what should we do?

00:17:12.830 --> 00:17:14.460
I'll use these to decide.

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:19.430
You're leaving it to luck.

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:22.520
I hold one coin in each hand.

00:17:22.930 --> 00:17:27.360
The coin that I keep in my hand is the door that I choose.

00:17:30.030 --> 00:17:36.900
Pegasus, I don't know what you're planning, but I'll never hand over Kaiba Corporation.

00:17:38.030 --> 00:17:41.230
You won't say that for long.

00:17:41.230 --> 00:17:42.460
What do you mean?

00:17:46.660 --> 00:17:47.800
Here I go!

00:17:59.660 --> 00:18:02.000
He revealed the Kyu coin.

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:04.730
Which means he kept the Mei coin.

00:18:04.980 --> 00:18:08.030
So you chose Mei.

00:18:08.030 --> 00:18:11.460
Damn!  What's the correct answer?

00:18:11.460 --> 00:18:13.460
Is it Mei?  Or is it...

00:18:13.460 --> 00:18:14.500
Kyu?

00:18:19.050 --> 00:18:20.530
The correct answer is...

00:18:20.900 --> 00:18:22.900
...the Kyu door!

00:18:25.630 --> 00:18:27.030
Oh no!

00:18:27.400 --> 00:18:28.620
That's what I thought.

00:18:29.200 --> 00:18:30.960
What's so funny?

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:34.300
This question has no correct answer.

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:38.440
If I choose Mei, you'll choose Kyu.

00:18:38.440 --> 00:18:40.670
If I choose Kyu, you'll choose Mei.

00:18:40.900 --> 00:18:43.730
I see!  That's not fair!

00:18:43.730 --> 00:18:47.100
But the fact remains that you couldn't answer the question!

00:18:47.100 --> 00:18:48.910
We win the game.

00:18:49.160 --> 00:18:52.460
I hate to break it to you, but I chose...

00:18:53.220 --> 00:18:54.310
Kyu!

00:18:55.730 --> 00:19:01.590
This coin didn't have Mei written on it.  It only had Kyu written on one side.

00:19:02.330 --> 00:19:07.100
The first coin had both Mei and Kyu written on it.

00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:14.030
Serves you right!

00:19:14.030 --> 00:19:19.370
I forgot to mention that one of my hands didn't tell the truth.

00:19:19.530 --> 00:19:23.660
All right!  Let's go into Pegasus's castle!

00:19:23.660 --> 00:19:24.640
Yeah!

00:19:41.730 --> 00:19:42.830
Mokuba!

00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:49.030
What's that?

00:19:49.220 --> 00:19:51.660
What did you do?

00:19:51.660 --> 00:19:53.960
Just a little magic trick.

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:55.880
Tell me what you did to Mokuba!

00:19:56.060 --> 00:19:59.220
This is a Soul Prison card.

00:19:59.220 --> 00:20:03.780
I'm keeping Mokuba boy's soul.

00:20:03.960 --> 00:20:05.060
What?

00:20:05.060 --> 00:20:09.500
If you want Mokuba boy back, you must defeat me in a duel.

00:20:09.860 --> 00:20:12.490
Fine!  I'll take you on right now!

00:20:13.760 --> 00:20:17.890
Challenge me now?  You're asking for too much.

00:20:17.890 --> 00:20:21.620
You must first duel Yugi boy.

00:20:21.620 --> 00:20:26.160
You can duel me if you defeat Yugi boy.

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:37.130
We escaped the Labyrinth Brothers' trap and made it to the surface.

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:42.700
Yugi is very trustworthy during a duel, but he's a bit unreliable otherwise.

00:20:42.700 --> 00:20:46.260
If we don't go to Pegasus's castle soon, we'll run out of time.

00:20:46.260 --> 00:20:49.400
Is that Kaiba standing in front of the castle?

00:20:49.400 --> 00:20:53.630
We have to duel if we want to enter the castle?

00:20:53.630 --> 00:20:57.660
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Duel of Destiny!
Yugi vs Kaiba

00:20:57.660 --> 00:20:59.300
Duel, standby!

00:21:02.690 --> 00:21:11.090
The flask glistens

00:21:12.130 --> 00:21:18.940
Wait for me in the science classroom

00:21:19.430 --> 00:21:27.920
If we put our cold hands together

00:21:28.620 --> 00:21:35.690
And rub them together, they become warm

00:21:37.390 --> 00:21:41.520
Shower of happiness

00:21:41.810 --> 00:21:45.630
I will shower you with it

00:21:45.960 --> 00:21:53.910
I will support you even when you feel lonely

00:21:54.110 --> 00:21:58.150
Shower of happiness

00:21:58.410 --> 00:22:02.270
You are not alone

00:22:02.650 --> 00:22:08.990
You're protected by a giant ring of friendship
